   NAME
	Handle - Pack a stage drawer into a LhASsA Parts Bin.

   FORMAT
	Handle FROM=<dir> NAME=<pkg> PRIMARY=<file> [VERSION=<ver>]
	       [OUT=<dir>] [FORCE] [QUIET] [HELP]

   TEMPLATE
	FROM,NAME,PRIMARY,VERSION/K,OUT/K,FORCE/S,QUIET/S,HELP/S

   PATH
	C:Handle

   FUNCTION
	Handle scans a stage directory and writes NAME.bin as a Parts
	Bin: an LHA archive with Manifest, -package.ver, Load.displayme,
	optional NAME.readme, and the staged payload. It also writes a
	Workbench Project icon NAME.bin.info (Parts box art) whose default
	tool is Load so double-click opens Load's confirm requester.

	Package mode is chosen from the FROM directory name:

	System package (FROM named SYS)
	    Subfolders are mapped to system destinations:

	        SDK/       -> SDK:
	        Libs/      -> LIBS:
	        Classes/   -> SYS:Classes/   (not CLASSES:)
	        Devs/      -> Devs:
	        L/         -> L:
	        C/         -> C:
	        Prefs/     -> SYS:Prefs/     (Prefs: is not a valid assign)
	        Tools/     -> SYS:Tools/     (Tools: is not a valid assign)
	        Locale/    -> LOCALE:
	        Help/      -> LOCALE:Help/  (HELP: assign target)
	        Fonts/     -> Fonts:

	    Archive members are stored under a SYS/ prefix
	    (for example SYS/Libs/foo.library).

	Application package (any other FROM name)
	    The tree is packed as ordinary folder and file names under
	    InstallRoot (Work:NAME/ by default, or TO= at Load time).
	    Names such as Libs/ or SDK/ are NOT remapped to system
	    locations -- they stay normal drawers in the app tree.

	Package Version comes from PRIMARY's $VER: tag, or from
	VERSION= when given. Each staged file is also scanned for $VER:;
	when found it is written on that File: line as Ver=major.minor
	or Ver=major.minor(dd.mm.yy) so Load can gate installs without
	extracting candidates first. Data files without $VER: simply
	omit Ver=.

	Secondary name tags select CPU/FPU variants, for example
	foo.library.020.881. Allowed tags: .020 .030 .040 .060 .881
	.882 .mmu .wos .pup (combinable; .wos and .pup cannot combine).

	Dot-prefixed names (.git, .svn, ...) are never packed.

   OPTIONS
	FROM=<dir>
	    Stage directory to scan (required). Name it SYS for a
	    system package; any other name for an application package.

	NAME=<pkg>
	    Package name and output base name (required). Writes
	    NAME.bin and NAME.bin.info.

	PRIMARY=<file>
	    File under FROM (or absolute path) whose $VER: supplies the
	    package version when VERSION= is omitted (required).

	VERSION=<ver>
	    Optional major.minor override for the package version.

	OUT=<dir>
	    Directory for the output archive (default: current dir).

	FORCE
	    Overwrite an existing output archive when present.

	QUIET
	    Reduce console output.

	HELP
	    Print this help text from HELP:<locale>/LhASsA/Handle.help
	    (falls back to HELP:english/LhASsA/Handle.help).

   EXAMPLES
	    1> Handle FROM=SYS NAME=FooLib PRIMARY=Libs/foo.library OUT=RAM:

	System package from a SYS stage; writes RAM:FooLib.bin with
	LIBS: destinations.

	    1> Handle FROM=MyAppStage NAME=MyApp PRIMARY=MyApp/MyApp VERSION=1.2

	Application package; drawers kept as normal names under
	Work:MyApp/.

   SEE ALSO
	Load, LhX, LhA
